<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="100" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>UAT round 5 (3) — richer "+ New" create forms: Matter (Name, Description, Matter Type, Practice Area, Assigned To Internal), Project (Name, Project Type, Description, Assigned To Internal), Invoice (Name, Description, Assigned To), created through the BFF quick-create</title>
    <phase>6 UAT round 5 (2026-10-05)</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Extends a BFF write path (`.cs`: quick-create request + record creation, reference lists) and the pane's create form (`.tsx`), with tests.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Write-path change on invariant-bearing tables (ownership, numbering, field mapping, assigned-to default) across BFF and client; schema facts must be verified live.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>UAT5-W2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Runs AFTER 099 (both edit `RelatedToPicker.tsx` / `SaveFlow.tsx`). Edits the BFF Office module — run `/conflict-check` first.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>099</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, frontend, office-addins, dataverse, record-creation, unit-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1.5 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Owner UAT round 5 (2026-10-05), item 3 + decisions B and C. Record: `notes/042-uat-round5-2026-10-05.md` §1-§3.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE full-stack developer: BFF Minimal API Office module (ADR-001/008/010) and the Office add-in pane (React 19, Fluent v9).</role>

  <goal>"+ New" creates a Matter, Project or Invoice with the fields the owner listed, through the existing BFF quick-create, so the new record is useful without opening Spaarke.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      - **Fields (owner item 3)** — Matter: Name, Description, Practice Area, Assigned To Internal (contact lookup); the
        existing required Matter Type stays. Project: Name, Project Type, Description, Assigned To Internal (contact
        lookup). Invoice: Name, Description, Assigned To (contact lookup).
      - **Decision B**: Assigned To is prefilled with the signed-in user's contact (the server's current default,
        `RecordCreationService.cs:255-288` / `AssignedToDefaults.cs`) and is **optional** — clearing it is allowed and
        the server then applies its existing default (state which). **Practice Area is required for a Matter**, like
        Matter Type.
      - **Decision C**: build the form from shared field components — `LookupField`
        (`Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/LookupField/LookupField.tsx`, host-agnostic, `onSearch` injected) by
        exact-path alias (task 096's mechanism) for the contact picker, backed by the existing contact search
        `GET /api/office/search/entities?type=Contact` (task 091). Practice Area and Project Type are dropdowns like
        Matter Type (`GET /api/office/search/matter-types`, `OfficeEndpoints.cs:1069`, task 038). Creation goes through
        the BFF quick-create (WP-3). Do NOT reuse the shared Create*Wizard steps (direct Dataverse writes, `Xrm`).
      - **Schema (from code, verify live with the Dataverse MCP before building)**: `sprk_matter` — `sprk_mattername`,
        `sprk_matterdescription`, `sprk_practicearea` → `sprk_practicearea_ref`, `sprk_mattertype` →
        `sprk_mattertype_ref`; `sprk_project` — `sprk_projectname`, `sprk_projectdescription`, project type →
        `sprk_projecttype_ref`; `sprk_invoice` — `sprk_name`, `sprk_description`. `sprk_assignedtointernal` is written as
        a **contact** lookup by the BFF, but `docs/data-model/sprk_matter-related-tables.md:23` says systemuser — resolve
        from live metadata. The Invoice "Assigned To" column is unknown — find it in live metadata.
      - **Server today**: `QuickCreateRequest.cs:31-105` (Name, Description, MatterTypeId, source record); Matter/Project
        through `RecordCreationService` (`:416-424`), Invoice through a separate minimal path. The pane sends
        `onCreateRecord(type, name, matterTypeId?)` (`RelatedToPicker.tsx:139`) — no description today.
    </background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner item 3 + decision B">Exactly the listed fields per type. Required: Name (all), Matter Type + Practice Area (Matter). Optional: Description, Project Type, Assigned To. Assigned To prefilled with the user's contact when one is linked; otherwise empty.</constraint>
    <constraint source="decision C / ADR-012 amended">Contact picker = shared `LookupField` by exact-path alias (never the barrel). Dropdown lists come from the BFF, load-once, same shape as matter types; prefer extending the existing matter-types route into one parameterized reference-list route over adding near-identical routes (CLAUDE.md §11) — state the choice.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002 / write path">All writes through the BFF quick-create. Existing invariants unchanged: ownership (I-6), autonumber (I-11), field mapping, container. A posted lookup id the caller cannot read is refused like other filing targets (reuse the existing access check; denied and not-found look the same).</constraint>
    <constraint source="schema">No new Dataverse column or table. If a field the owner listed has no column (e.g. Invoice Assigned To), ESCALATE (trigger 1) — do not create schema.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">BFF obligations: placement stated; publish size measured master-vs-branch from fresh SHORT-path worktrees (Compress-Archive Optimal, equal file counts); CVE check; tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` and contract tests for the request.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-10 / ADR-021">Same form in both hosts; Fluent v9 tokens; fits at 320 px; required markers and validation messages accessible.</constraint>
    <constraint source="099">Keep 099's create-focus behaviour (only the create form shows while creating).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Matter form shows Name*, Description, Matter Type*, Practice Area*, Assigned To Internal (prefilled); Create stays disabled until the required fields are set; the created row carries every value entered.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Project form shows Name*, Project Type, Description, Assigned To Internal (prefilled); the created row carries every value entered.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Invoice form shows Name*, Description, Assigned To; the created row carries every value entered (or the task escalated on a missing column).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Clearing Assigned To creates the record with the server's stated default; a contact id the caller cannot read is refused (403/404 indistinguishable) and nothing is created.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Practice Area and Project Type lists load from the BFF; a failed load shows a retry message, never an empty required field that blocks silently.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Existing behaviour unchanged: numbering, ownership, field mapping and the 404/409 handling of quick-create (existing tests green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Gates: BFF build 0/0; Office test scopes + ArchTests green; gated jest green; lint 0; typecheck 0 production; publish-size delta reported; CVE clean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Live (after deploy): create one Matter, Project and Invoice from the pane with every field; open each in Spaarke and see the values. If unavailable, leave open.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A listed field has no Dataverse column, or `sprk_assignedtointernal` targets a different table than the BFF assumes — STOP and report.</trigger>
    <trigger>`/conflict-check` shows another active project editing `RecordCreationService.cs` / `QuickCreateRequest.cs` / `OfficeEndpoints.cs` — coordinate before editing.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>`/conflict-check`; verify the schema live (Dataverse MCP); read the quick-create request/service, the matter-types route and the pane's create form.</step>
    <step>BFF: request fields, reference lists, access check, creation; tests.</step>
    <step>Pane: per-type forms with `LookupField` + dropdowns; tests.</step>
    <step>Gates, publish size; `notes/100-create-record-fields.md`; POML status.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>The BFF quick-create (`QuickCreateRequest`, `RecordCreationService`), the matter-types list route, the contact search route and the shared `LookupField` exist.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — adds fields to the existing request and form, and generalizes the existing reference-list route; no new service or component.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A record created from the pane has only a name (and matter type), so the user must open Spaarke to finish it (owner, round 5 item 3).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Create forms">
      <steps>
        <step>"+ New" → Matter: fill every field; Create enabled only when required ones are set; the new Matter shows the values in Spaarke.</step>
        <step>Same for Project and Invoice.</step>
      </steps>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

